Subject: Add the kdos_crt full-screen CRT effect

kdos_crt is a built-in effect that paints each output into an offscreen
texture and draws it back through a CRT shader: a three-tap phosphor bleed,
scanlines on every third row, a vignette, barrel curvature and a faint floor
in the accent colour. It plays a 400 ms degauss when the colour scheme's
accent changes, collapses the screen to a line and a dot when the session
locks or quits, and exports that power-down as io.kdos.Crt1 at /io/kdos/Crt1.

It is off by default, refuses software rendering and HDR outputs, leaves
screenshots, screencasts and the colour picker the plain picture, stands
aside while zoom or the magnifier is active, and with Fullscreen=false hands
an active fullscreen window's output back to direct scanout. A built-in
effect is a static plugin and so is not refused at a point release the way
an out-of-tree effect is.

